**Facts verified directly against the clone** (git commands were permission-blocked in `/tmp/mowglinext-src`, so I read `.git` metadata, decompressed the packfile via a copied `.git`, and read sources):

- **Repo/commit**: `https://github.com/mowglinext/mowglinext` @ `faf658bc57b92410ee820adff9953e663b5b0230` — "Merge pull request #624 from mowglinext/dev", Tue 2026-09-15 21:37:56 +0200; submodules universal-gnss @ `ab32f67`, opennav_coverage @ `d6e41a2`; release v1.4.0 = `4fcabb3`
- **Major packages**: 12 colcon packages (`mowgli_interfaces` 16 msg/15 srv/3 action, `mowgli_hardware`, `mowgli_bringup`, `mowgli_localization`, `fusion_graph`, `mowgli_nav2_plugins`, `mowgli_behavior`, `mowgli_coverage`, `mowgli_map`, `mowgli_monitoring`, `mowgli_leds`, `mowgli_simulation`) + 2 submodules
- **Driver coverage**: `/gps/fix` (um960 `/fix`), `/imu/data` + `/imu/mag_raw` (wit `/imu`), `/wheel_odom` (mcu `/odom`), `/battery_state` (mcu `/battery`), `/cmd_vel` already stamped — all rename-only; plus the duplicate-`/imu` and driver-TF conflicts, and the unsatisfied surface (`/hardware_bridge/{status,emergency,power}`, `/wheel_ticks`, `/gps/status` as `GnssStatus`, driver services, etc.)
- **Porting**: MCU framing table (COBS+CRC16 vs `A5…5A`+module-id dispatch), message-schema gap list, GNSS (UM960 unsupported by universal-gnss), Lyrical→Humble deltas
- **Web UI**: Go/Gin backend (`gui/main.go`, Go 1.25) + React 19/Vite/antd frontend, served at `http://<ip>:4006`, ROS access via Foxglove WebSocket `:8765` + teleop relay `:8766`, host-networked `mowgli-gui` container
- **Docker plan**: `Dockerfile.mowgli` derived from `mower:humble`, `mowgli_src` named volume (or bind-mount `/tmp/mowglinext-src/ros2/src`), a full `docker-compose.mowgli.yml` override with matching `ROS_DOMAIN_ID`/CycloneDDS, build/run/verify commands, and a milestone sequence

Corrections made vs. the previous draft: commit/message/date verified from the packfile, `mower_interfaces` is 7 msg/**4 srv** (not 1 srv), GUI entry is `gui/main.go` (not `cmd/mowgli-updater`), and QoS notes fixed (our `/battery`//`odom` are RELIABLE; only the IMU publishers are BEST_EFFORT).
